XARGS(1)                    User Commands                   XARGS(1)

NAME
    xargs - build and execute command lines from standard input

SYNOPSIS
    xargs [-0rt] [-n count] [-s size] [-I replace] [command [argument...]]

DESCRIPTION
    xargs parses quoted, backslash-escaped, whitespace-separated input and
    appends items to command. The default command is echo.

OPTIONS
    -0           read NUL-separated items without quote processing
    -n count     use at most count input items per invocation
    -s size      limit the approximate command-line byte count
    -r           do not run the command when input is empty
    -t           print each command before executing it
    -I replace   read one item per line and replace occurrences in arguments

EXIT STATUS
    0 indicates success, 123 a command failure, 126 an unexecutable command,
    and 127 a command that could not be found.

SEE ALSO
    find(1)
